keel-overlay-vip (0.1.1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Every unit is off on the first installation, like the other overlays
    (handbook decision 0041). keel-vip-check.timer was enabled by
    dh_installsystemd, whose was-enabled defaults to true and which does not
    read the preset, so a standalone machine ran the check every minute.
    The timer now has no [Install]: keel-vip.service wants it and it is
    PartOf the controller, so the check runs exactly while keel spec apply
    keeps the VIP enabled, and stops with it. Both units are installed with
    --no-enable --no-start and both are disabled in the preset.
    tests/overlay-install.bats installs the package on a booted trixie
    machine and asserts both are disabled and inactive.

 -- KeelLinux maintainers <admin@keellinux.org>  Wed, 07 Oct 2026 23:22:41 +0000

keel-overlay-vip (0.1.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * First release: the units of keel's service VIP on the WireGuard mesh
    (handbook decision 0049, third round). keel-vip.service runs keel vip
    tend, the root helper, with CAP_NET_ADMIN alone, AF_UNIX and
    AF_NETLINK only, writing only /var/lib/keel/vip and /etc/wireguard;
    it starts the controller as a transient unit with a dynamic user and
    no capability, and drops every VIP the node carries once it stops;
    StartLimitIntervalSec=0, so a crash loop never leaves it stopped for
    good; installed disabled.
    keel-vip-check.timer runs keel vip check at boot and every minute.

 -- Marcos Mendez <mendez.foto@gmail.com>  Wed, 07 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
